# Hodge coverage family: a Hodge decomposition is defined only relative to a
# complete, declared frame — the signal, its exact/coexact/harmonic components,
# its boundary operator, its carrier sheaf, the exact residual witnessing
# reconstruction (signal = exact + coexact + harmonic, residual 0/1), and the
# three exact pairwise-orthogonality inner products (each 0/1). Every obligation
# is a qualified-cardinality + allValuesFrom OWL restriction (EL-safe) that
# derives the paired sh:minCount/maxCount + sh:class property shape; a missing or
# wrongly typed component fails the derived constraint and isolates
# math:IncompleteHodgeDecomposition. Omitting the boundary operator fails the
# derived QualifiedMinCount, the malformed-boundary-operator counterexample.
math:HodgeDecomposition logic:subClassOf
    [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty math:decomposesFlow ; owl:minQualifiedCardinality 1 ; owl:onClass math:MathematicalObject ] ,
